    ENG-2231 Candidate node tag not formatted with Obsidian version 1.13.7 Linux (#1416)

    * ENG-2231 Colour discourse node tags with a CodeMirror decoration

    Tag colours were applied by a MutationObserver stamping data attributes and
    CSS custom properties onto CodeMirror's own hashtag spans. CodeMirror owns
    those elements and recreates them on focus and as lines scroll through the
    viewport, which silently discarded the styling document-wide.

    Replace it with a CM6 ViewPlugin emitting mark decorations, which CodeMirror
    re-applies on every update. Tags are located through the syntax tree rather
    than by matching `#...` in the text, so Obsidian's own rules about what counts
    as a tag (code blocks, URL fragments, headings) are inherited.

    A mark decoration can only create a span inside Obsidian's `.cm-hashtag`, which
    is the element carrying the tag's padding and border radius, so the per-node
    colours live in a generated stylesheet that targets the parent via `:has()`.

    Also resolves the tagged line through `posAtDOM` instead of searching the
    document for matching text, which rewrote the wrong line when a document
    repeated it, and repaints tags when node type settings change.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

